# Go Life - AI Agents Service (LangChain + LangSmith)

## Project Context

You are working on **Go Life**, a mobile app that creates a personalized digital avatar. This is the **AI Agents** service - the intelligence brain, built with **LangChain** and monitored with **LangSmith**.

### Architecture Overview

```
Mobile App → API-BACKEND (Django) → AI-AGENTS (this - LangChain)
                                          ↓
                                    PostgreSQL + pgvector
                                    LangSmith (observability)
                                    OpenAI / Anthropic (LLMs)
```

### Your Responsibilities

- Generate avatar responses using LangChain (OpenAI/Claude)
- Manage avatar memory with LangChain Memory components
- Extract insights using LangChain chains
- Generate and search embeddings with LangChain
- Build personalized prompts with LangChain PromptTemplates
- Monitor all LLM calls with LangSmith
- Sentiment and emotion analysis

### NOT Your Responsibilities

- User authentication (api-backend does this)
- Social network connections (api-backend does this)
- Storing conversations (api-backend does this)

---

## Tech Stack

```
Runtime:        Python 3.11+
Framework:      FastAPI 0.100+
LLM Framework:  LangChain 0.1+
Observability:  LangSmith
LLM Providers:  langchain-openai, langchain-anthropic
Embeddings:     LangChain Embeddings (OpenAI, etc.)
Vector Store:   LangChain pgvector integration
Validation:     Pydantic v2
ORM:            SQLAlchemy 2.0 (async)
Database:       PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector
Cache:          Redis
Type Checking:  Pyright (strict mode)
Linting:        Ruff
Formatting:     Black + isort
Testing:        Pytest + pytest-asyncio
```

